   "source": [
    "We use two metrics to determine the optimal number of clusters for our GMM: the **Bayesian Information Criterion (BIC)** and the **Silhouette Score**.\n",
    "\n",
    "* The **BIC** penalizes model complexity while rewarding goodness of fit. It is the natural model selection criterion for GMMs, analogous to the Elbow Method used for KMeans.\n",
    "* The **Silhouette Score** is a model-agnostic metric that measures how well each data point fits within its assigned cluster relative to neighboring clusters. It can be applied to any clustering algorithm, including GMM, by using the hard cluster assignments from `predict()`."
   ]
  },
